==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/bɪŋ/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/bɪŋ/|[biŋ]|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-au-bing.ogg|Audio (AU)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪŋ|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|bing}}, {{m|enm|binge}}, {{m|enm|benge}}, from {{der|en|non|bingr||heap of corn; bed; bolster}}, cognate with {{cog|sco|bing}}, {{cog|sv|binge||heap}}, {{cog|da|bing||bin; box; compartment}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|slang}} Prison [[solitary confinement]], a term used by inmates.
# {{lb|en|British}} A [[heap]] or [[pile]], such as a [[slag heap]].

===Etymology 2===
Origin obscure. Compare {{cog|sco|bin||to move speedily with noise}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|dated|_|slang|or|dialectal}} To [[go]]; [[walk]]; [[come]]; [[run]]

===Etymology 3===
[[onomatopoeia|Onomatopoeia]] of a bouncing sound.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|ping}}
* {{l|en|ding}}
* {{l|en|bong}}

====Interjection====
{{en-interj}}

# {{lb|en|onomatopoeia}} {{non-gloss definition|The sound made by a bounce, or by striking a metallic surface}}

